```
:::
:::


Without `select=`, every node of every match is selected, which for this pattern is
everyone connected to The Matrix, and the movie itself:

::: {#0096bafa .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
graph.select_match(
    "MATCH (m:Movie {title: $title})--(p)",
    params={"title": "The Matrix"},
    set_op="replace",
)
sorted(graph.get_label_from_id(i) for i in graph.get_selected_node_ids())
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```
['Carrie-Anne Moss', 'Keanu Reeves', 'Lana Wachowski', 'matrix']
```
:::
:::


Only John Wick is left out, since Keanu Reeves is the one link between the two movies:

::: {#58d73d7e .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
spots = {
    "Carrie-Anne Moss": (0, 2), "Keanu Reeves": (3, 2),
    "Lana Wachowski": (0, 0), "matrix": (1.5, 1), "wick": (4.5, 1),
}
graph.set_node_attrs(
    "pos", {graph.get_id_from_label(v): p for v, p in spots.items()}
)

graph.plot(
    layout="pos", highlight="selection", label_by="label", height=240
)
```

